        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add managed sandbox lifecycle",
        "body": "Closes #98516\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nLong-running digital-employee and team-operations sessions can need an isolated sandbox that persists across turns in the same owner scope, but still gets cleaned up deterministically when the owning session resets, is deleted, rolls over, or becomes stale. Before this change, session-scope sandbox ownership and cleanup semantics were not managed as one lifecycle, which made deterministic reuse and terminal cleanup harder to reason about for operators.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds an opt-in managed lifecycle for ephemeral session-owned sandboxes using the existing sandbox backend, Docker, registry, workspace, and reset/session primitives. The implementation records lifecycle ownership, locks scope cleanup, reuses the same sandbox inside the owner scope, blocks conflicting reset/delete/compaction work while cleanup is pending, removes terminal runtime/workspace resources, and keeps idle/age pruning as crash-recovery retry behavior.\n\nAI-assisted implementation disclosure: this draft was prepared with AI assistance. No transcript attachment is included.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can enable session-scoped sandboxing for long-running agents and expect stable reuse within a session owner plus deterministic cleanup on reset/delete/rollover. Sandboxing remains opt-in; this does not introduce a global default sandbox requirement or a breaking runtime default.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused issue-first gate: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/98516\n- Branch/head: `codex/managed-sandbox-lifecycle` at `87ac76653d217d6b7560257102a1eb0c4856b3f5`\n- Local post-rebase focused tests: `PATH=/Users/steipete/.cache/codex-runtimes/codex-primary-runtime/dependencies/node/bin:/Users/steipete/.cache/codex-runtimes/codex-primary-runtime/dependencies/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/server.sessions.compaction.test.ts src/agents/sandbox/prune.test.ts src/agents/sandbox/lifecycle.test.ts` -> 2 Vitest shards, 54 tests passed.\n- Local focused lifecycle surface before rebase: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs` over sandbox lifecycle/scope/registry/prune/manage/SSH/Docker/media/session/gateway/extension tests -> 6 Vitest shards, 755 tests passed.\n- Blacksmith Testbox exact-head Docker lifecycle scenario: `tbx_01kwfsm0ghknxt7qfpe945k9w8`, provider `blacksmith-testbox`, Actions https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28549202714, passed. Marker: `DOCKER_LIFECYCLE_PROOF`, head `87ac76653d217d6b7560257102a1eb0c4856b3f5`, reused `true`, removed 1 container and 1 workspace, 0 failures.\n- Blacksmith Testbox changed gate on exact branch head: `tbx_01kwfs806qdy3zdybdmmj1nmqj`, provider `blacksmith-testbox`, Actions https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28548859859. It failed only in core test typecheck for `src/commands/daemon-install-helpers.test.ts`, which this PR does not touch.\n- Current-main proof for the changed-gate blocker: `tbx_01kwfscbzbkc4b0c3vh67jx9h0`, provider `blacksmith-testbox`, Actions https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28548971551, exact main `eb417fa206e6ec76df12c500d08f8fd8691298e9`; reproduced the same `src/commands/daemon-install-helpers.test.ts` TS2741/TS2322 failures. This PR does not patch that unrelated mainline failure.\n- Fresh autoreview: `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode branch --base origin/main --codex-bin /Applications/Codex.app/Contents/Resources/codex` -> clean, no accepted/actionable findings.\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` -> passed.\n\n## Risks / Non-goals\n\n- Main advanced after the one requested local rebase; this draft intentionally does not chase unrelated main commits.\n- Required CI may inherit the current-main `daemon-install-helpers` test-type failure until main is fixed.\n- No UI or visual surface changed; no screenshots are applicable.\n- This does not change the global sandbox default.\n",
